course: dictionary
lesson: 14562
title: Who is a physicist?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A physicist is a scientist who studies physics. Physics is the science of matter, energy, forces, light, sound, electricity and how the universe works.
explain: Look at the word parts: physic-ist. The ending -ist means a person who does or studies something, like a scientist or a pianist. So a physicist is a person who studies physics.
explain: Physicists ask questions such as: why do things fall to the ground? What is light made of? They test their ideas with experiments, and they work in labs, universities, space agencies and hospitals.
explain: Some famous physicists are Isaac Newton, who studied gravity, Marie Curie, who studied radioactivity, Albert Einstein, who studied relativity, and Stephen Hawking, who studied black holes.
fact: A physicist is a scientist who studies physics.
fact: Physics is the science of matter, energy, forces, light, sound, electricity and how the universe works.
fact: «The physicist measured how fast the ball fell.» Physicists measure things carefully.
fact: Physicists work in labs, universities, space agencies and hospitals.
fact: The plural of physicist is physicists: «Two physicists shared the prize.»
exercise: «The physicist measured how fast the ball fell.» What is a physicist? | A writer of stories | A person who sells ice cream | *A scientist who studies physics | A sports player who runs very fast
exercise: What does physics study? | Only plants and animals | Paintings and art | The history of kings and queens | *Matter, energy, forces, light and sound
exercise: Which famous physicist studied gravity? | Roald Dahl | Charles Dickens | Marie Curie | *Isaac Newton
test: «Dr Amara is a physicist who builds tiny sensors for space rockets.» Where might a physicist like Dr Amara work? | Only in a school kitchen | *In a lab, a university or a space agency | On a farm, milking cows | In a shoe shop
test: Which word means more than one physicist? | physic | *physicists | physicistly | physicals
exam: Why would a physicist use a lab? | To bake cakes for the class | *To test ideas about matter, energy and forces | To teach dance moves | To sell tickets at the zoo
